  "content": {
    "body": "A **skill** pebble is a reusable PROCEDURE — a HOW-TO the AI runs, exposed\nas a `/slash-command` in chat. It answers \"HOW to do X\": a named recipe\nwith a trigger, inputs, an ordered set of steps, allowed tools, a success\ncheck, and an output contract. Skills are AI-side DOCTRINE — authored, not\nderived from code. This doc DEFINES every component; AGENTS reference\nskills to gain capabilities.\n\n## Skill vs Agent — the difference (read this first)\n\n- A **skill** is a PROCEDURE — a verb, the reusable HOW: steps, inputs,\n  tools, verify, output. It is INVOKED (as a /command) and executes when\n  triggered. It does not decide WHETHER to act.\n- An **agent** is a PERSONA — a noun, the WHO: a role with judgment, voice,\n  boundaries, escalation, constraints, and the SKILLS it may use. It brings\n  expertise and DECIDES; it USES skills to act.\n- Relationship: an agent HAS / USES skills; a skill is USED BY agents. Put\n  PROCEDURE in a skill (steps); put JUDGMENT / expertise / voice in an agent\n  (instructions). Litmus: writing \"first do X, then Y\" → a skill; writing\n  \"who this is and how they weigh trade-offs\" → an agent.\n\n## Pebble-level components\n\n- **name** — the skill's name; it is ALSO its `/slash-command`.\n- **status** — AI-side lifecycle: Draft (`planned`) → Active (`verified`) →\n  Inactive (`deprecated`). A skill is authored and activated, not \"built\".\n- **description** — one-line summary (mirrors `purpose`).\n- **references** — a skill references the **rules** it must follow and the\n  **knowledge** it needs as context. It does NOT reference models /\n  structures / findings / code — those are the codebase a skill operates\n  ON, reached through the steps, not linked here.\n- **resources** — NONE. A skill is AI doctrine, not codebase; `link-code`\n  is refused on it.\n\n## Content components — the categories under a skill\n\n- **purpose** — one line: what the skill does.\n- **whenToUse** — the trigger: the conditions under which an agent reaches\n  for it.\n- **arguments** — what the invocation accepts, e.g. \"<ticket-id> [--draft]\".\n- **prerequisites** — what must be true / available BEFORE running (access,\n  files, state).\n- **tools** — the tools the skill may use, e.g. \"Read, Edit, Bash(git *)\";\n  empty = no restriction.\n- **steps** — the ordered procedure (the core of the skill).\n- **constraints** — hard must / never rules for the procedure.\n- **verify** — how the agent PROVES success before declaring done (the\n  check — distinct from output, which is the what).\n- **onFailure** — what to do when a step fails: recovery, escalation,\n  report.\n- **output** — what the skill produces + the definition of done.\n- **examples** — few-shot input → output pairs.\n\n## Quick map — component → what's under it\n\n| Component | Under it |\n|---|---|\n| pebble.name | skill name = its /slash-command |\n| pebble.status | Draft (planned) · Active (verified) · Inactive (deprecated) |\n| references | rules (must follow) + knowledge (context) |\n| resources | NONE (AI doctrine, not codebase) |\n| purpose | one line: what it does |\n| whenToUse | trigger conditions |\n| arguments | invocation inputs |\n| prerequisites | preconditions (access/files/state) |\n| tools | allowed tools, or unrestricted |\n| steps | the ordered procedure |\n| constraints | hard must/never rules |\n| verify | success check before done |\n| onFailure | recovery / escalation |\n| output | product + definition of done |\n| examples | input → output pairs |\n\n## Skill CLI — all skill operations live here\n\nA skill's content kind is **skill**. `content` is written WHOLE (authored\nprose — presence-checked, not field-validated like models). Every skill\npebble becomes a `/slash-command` in chat.\n\nCREATE a skill:\n\n    pebbles-cli create skills --title \"Trace a ticket\" --content '{\n      \"kind\": \"skill\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Map a ticket to the exact files and flow it touches\",\n      \"whenToUse\": \"Before implementing or reviewing a scoped ticket\",\n      \"arguments\": \"<ticket-id> [--deep]\",\n      \"prerequisites\": [{ \"text\": \"Linear + GitHub access\" }],\n      \"tools\": \"Read, Grep, Glob, Bash(git *)\",\n      \"steps\": [\n        { \"text\": \"Read the ticket and its linked PRs / specs\" },\n        { \"text\": \"map-search the domain terms; open the top files\" },\n        { \"text\": \"Trace the flow end to end; list every affected file\" }\n      ],\n      \"constraints\": [{ \"text\": \"Read-only — never modify code in this skill\" }],\n      \"verify\": [{ \"text\": \"Every acceptance criterion maps to a real file:line\" }],\n      \"output\": \"A discovery report: files, flow, gaps\"\n    }'\n\nREFERENCE the rules + knowledge it relies on — from Properties → References,\nor set `refs` via `update --patch` (targets are rule / knowledge pebbles).\n\nSTATUS / inspect / retire:\n\n    pebbles-cli set-status skills/trace-a-ticket.pebble verified      # Active\n    pebbles-cli refs skills/trace-a-ticket.pebble\n    pebbles-cli get skills/trace-a-ticket.pebble\n    pebbles-cli set-status skills/trace-a-ticket.pebble deprecated     # retire (no delete)\n\n## Method lives elsewhere\n\nThis doc DEFINES the components. See the **agent-reference** doc for the\npersona that USES skills, and **skills-and-agents** for how the two compose\nat runtime.",
    "kind": "text"
  },
